        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "eda07afc-1bc5-3e93-8d61-87bf99fa5e30",
                "word": "inique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9e168c8d-8fe2-4d64-bfbe-cf1d6a363097",
                        "entry_id": "eda07afc-1bc5-3e93-8d61-87bf99fa5e30",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "iniques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e089a907-b2aa-34a4-9a75-f8ea0bf684c9",
                        "entry_id": "eda07afc-1bc5-3e93-8d61-87bf99fa5e30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui n'est pas juste, pas égal ; qui manque d’équité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e467bc5-5559-49ee-bd73-30518e7cf36a",
                                "sense_id": "e089a907-b2aa-34a4-9a75-f8ea0bf684c9",
                                "text": "La masse croit qu'elle souffre parce qu'elle subit une inique conséquence d'un passé qui était plein de violences, d'ignorance et de méchanceté."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b1249a9-3e90-4c7a-aa45-62c97d015d3f",
                                "sense_id": "e089a907-b2aa-34a4-9a75-f8ea0bf684c9",
                                "text": "Mais, à la longue, elle se vit contrainte de renoncer à ses méthodes iniques, parce que trop d'enquêtes s'étaient tournées à sa confusion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b283bc20-5f4e-4380-aa58-1a70efeb51c3",
                                "sense_id": "e089a907-b2aa-34a4-9a75-f8ea0bf684c9",
                                "text": "L’article 745.51 des conservateurs s’avère inique. Il est choquant que le gouvernement Trudeau n’ait pas corrigé la situation et ait abandonné ses responsabilités aux juges."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dd75743a-ebc4-3bf7-b1cf-97b3579a353b",
                        "entry_id": "eda07afc-1bc5-3e93-8d61-87bf99fa5e30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est injuste en parlant des personnes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "485b8494-84cd-4b11-bf1b-9c4fe5f60351",
                                "sense_id": "dd75743a-ebc4-3bf7-b1cf-97b3579a353b",
                                "text": "Il s’est montré inique envers cet innocent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e303f7f8-5c6e-41bf-b81a-a52e05ef7222",
                        "source_entry_id": "eda07afc-1bc5-3e93-8d61-87bf99fa5e30",
                        "target_lang_word": "iniquitous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "iniquitous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cb7affc-a173-3b55-ab65-0ea12ce155e6",
                                        "entry_id": "88ad2a07-8556-3fee-bebe-bb3e5f1036e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterized by iniquity (“deviation from what is right”).",
                                            "Morally objectionable; sinful, wicked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "822a6aea-13c7-4def-833a-90037694cb20",
                                                "sense_id": "4cb7affc-a173-3b55-ab65-0ea12ce155e6",
                                                "text": "\"It certainly is a most iniquitous affair,\" said Mr. Bennet, \"and nothing can clear Mr. Collins from the guilt of inheriting Longbourn. But if you will listen to his letter, you may perhaps be a little softened by his manner of expressing himself.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "295457be-67ff-4f6c-8ef2-7fe1ff325713",
                                                "sense_id": "4cb7affc-a173-3b55-ab65-0ea12ce155e6",
                                                "text": "Are you aware, sir, that we have gone to enormous expense to resist this iniquitous attempt of yours?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d1a8617-af12-4643-8410-31fe6eec6da3",
                                                "sense_id": "4cb7affc-a173-3b55-ab65-0ea12ce155e6",
                                                "text": "The storm-centre of a combined newspaper attack lasting for months, Daylight's character had been torn to shreds. There was no fact in his history that had not been distorted into a criminality or a vice. This public making of him over into an iniquitous monster had pretty well crushed any lingering hope he had of getting acquainted with Dede Mason."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5f09024-19ec-3b49-a070-bed55238f9f4",
                                        "entry_id": "88ad2a07-8556-3fee-bebe-bb3e5f1036e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterized by iniquity (“deviation from what is right”).",
                                            "Grossly unfair or unjust."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b952fb84-2499-471d-b7d0-ee33e873c611",
                                                "sense_id": "c5f09024-19ec-3b49-a070-bed55238f9f4",
                                                "text": "It is a Maxim among theſe Men, That vvhatever has been done before may legally be done again: And therefore they take ſpecial Care to record all the Deciſions formerly made, even thoſe vvhich have through Ignorance or Corruption contradicted the Rules of common Juſtice, and the general Reaſon of Mankind. Theſe, under the Name of Precedents, they produce as Authorities, and thereby endeavour to juſtify the moſt iniquitous Opinions; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e7824e6-ba51-4ea0-bdbc-031a81d28b0c",
                                                "sense_id": "c5f09024-19ec-3b49-a070-bed55238f9f4",
                                                "text": "[Judicial independence] operates as a check upon the legiſlative body in paſſing them [unjust and partial laws]; vvho, perceiving that obſtacles to the ſucceſs of an iniquitous intention are to be expected from the ſcruples of the courts, are in a manner compelled by the very motives of the injuſtice they mediate, to qualify their attempts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be167bf6-0d30-4858-93ab-484b68e8e253",
                                                "sense_id": "c5f09024-19ec-3b49-a070-bed55238f9f4",
                                                "text": "The majority of the jury which tried Barbara Napier, having acquitted her of attendance at the North Berwick meeting, were themselves threatened with a trial for wilful error upon an assize, and could only escape from severe censure and punishment by pleading Guilty, and submitting themselves to the king's pleasure. This rigorous and iniquitous conduct shows a sufficient reason why there should be so few acquittals from a charge of witchcraft, where the juries were so much at the mercy of the Crown."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9ec764f-fb58-4db0-8351-25175d317118",
                                                "sense_id": "c5f09024-19ec-3b49-a070-bed55238f9f4",
                                                "text": "There had been a good deal of dealers' yea and nay about it [a watercolour painting], whether it was for sale or not; it was a smaller drawing than most of the England and Wales series, and there were many hints in the market about its being iniquitous in price."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d64e3eb8-d7e4-4821-b0e7-2351db909359",
                                                "sense_id": "c5f09024-19ec-3b49-a070-bed55238f9f4",
                                                "text": "I've had it. That's it George! For one year now, I've been providing X-rated entertainment and you reciprocate with PG! It's an iniquitous arrangement!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
